 Probably should rather use method = â€˜qrâ€™ !?␀rankMatrix(x, method=â€˜qrâ€™): computing t(x) as nrow(x) < ncol(x)␀readMM(): column indices â€˜jâ€™ are not in 1:ncol[=%d]␀readMM(): expected %d entries but found only %d␀readMM(): row indices â€˜iâ€™ are not in 1:nrow[=%d]␀recycled %s would have maximal index exceeding %s␀replacement diagonal has incompatible type "%s"␀replacement diagonal has wrong length␀replacement has length zero␀representation â€˜%sâ€™ not recognized␀row indices must be <= nrow(.) which is %d␀should never happen ...␀subscript out of bounds␀subscripts exceeding %s replaced with NA␀such indexing must be by logical or 2-column numeric matrix␀sum(<abIndex>) is not yet implemented␀suppressing %d columns␀suppressing %d columns and %d rows␀suppressing %d rows␀symmetric matrix must be square␀symmetry form â€˜%sâ€™ is not yet implemented␀symmetry form â€˜%sâ€™ not recognized␀symmetry form â€˜hermitianâ€™ not yet implemented for reading␀symmetry form â€˜skew-symmetricâ€™ not yet implemented for reading␀the %d-th (sub)-diagonal (k = %d) is too short; filling with NA's␀the default value of argument â€˜%sâ€™ of method â€˜%s(<%s>, <%s>)â€™ may change from %s to %s as soon as the next release of Matrix; set â€˜%sâ€™ when programming␀too many arguments␀too many replacement values␀triangular matrix must be square␀trimmed means are not defined for complex data␀type â€˜%sâ€™ not recognized␀unexpected %s="%s" in â€˜%sâ€™ method␀uniDiag=TRUE, but not all diagonal entries are 1␀uniDiag=TRUE, not all entries in diagonal coded as 1␀use Diagonal() to construct diagonal (symmetric && triangular) sparse matrices␀using	 "old code" part in  Csparse subassignment␀using"old code" part in Csparse subassignment
